<title>MALAYSIA: Tongkah eyes finance company.</title>
<headline>Tongkah eyes finance company.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-11-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Malaysia's Tongkah Holdings Bhd said on Wednesday that it has received permission from the central bank, Bank Negara Malaysia, to start negotiations to acquire a majority stake in a finance company.</p>
<p>It said in a brief statement that it plans to acquire from Perdana Merchant Bankers Bhd its entire 88 percent equity interest in Perdana Finance Bhd.</p>
<p>Pending the conclusion of negotiations, Tongkah has requested that trading of its shares continue to be suspended.</p>
<p>Shares of Tongkah, suspended since October 28, were last traded at 4.34 ringgit.</p>
<p>Tongkah's businesses include a brokerage firm, an interest in an Internet service provider, hospitals and a seismic data processing company.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603 230 8911)</p>
